  "title": "Erdős Problem #1091",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $G$ be a $K_4$-free graph with chromatic number $4$. Must $G$ contain an odd cycle with at least two diagonals?\nMore generally, is there some $f(r)\\to \\infty$ such that every graph with chromatic number $4$, in which every subgraph on $\\leq r$ vertices has chromatic number $\\leq 3$, contains an odd cycle with at least $f(r)$ diagonals?",
